  ($id$sust-h-95$id$, $sec$calculo-integral$sec$, $sub$sustitucion-trigonometrica$sub$, $law$sustitucion-trigonometrica$law$, $diff$hard$diff$, $prompt$Calcula usando $x = 7\tan\theta$: $\int \frac{dx}{\sqrt{x^2 + 49}}$$prompt$, $json$[{"latex":"\\ln\\left|\\frac{x}{7} + \\sqrt{x^2 + 49}\\right| + C","correct":false},{"latex":"\\sqrt{x^2 + 49} + C","correct":false},{"latex":"\\frac{1}{7}\\arctan\\left(\\frac{x}{7}\\right) + C","correct":false},{"latex":"\\ln\\left|x + \\sqrt{x^2 + 49}\\right| + C","correct":true}]$json$::jsonb, $exp$Con $x = 7\tan\theta, dx = 7\sec^2\theta\,d\theta$, la integral queda $\int \sec\theta\,d\theta = \ln|\sec\theta + \tan\theta| + C' = \ln|x + \sqrt{x^2 + 49}| + C$.$exp$),
